History
1.1.1  Closer to GitHub: code, **bold** and links in one heading; code
     in headings at heading size; markers without a partner ("made with
     ***.") stay text; links to "../file.md" in the parent drawer; links
     to the second heading of a name (#name-1); "1. [x]" keeps its
     number; [!note] in small letters; all Latin-1 entities (&auml;) and
     more. The "i" in H2 headings has its dot again. Numbers of a list
     were missing with wide system fonts (TTF=0).
     Thanks to the author of Dash for the report.
1.1  (Not on Aminet, sent to testers only.)
     Links to HTML anchors work: [text](#name) goes to the tag with
     id="name" or name="name" (<a id="name"></a>, <h2 id="name"> ...),
     as many documents on GitHub use them. Headings that are code
     (### `function(x)`) are drawn bold, as headings.
     Lines can be marked with the mouse and copied as plain text with
     MultiView's "Copy": paragraphs come as one line, list items with
     their markers, table cells with tabs between them. "Copy", "Save
     As" and "Clear Selected" are enabled in MultiView's menus now (the
     datatype did not tell MultiView that it can do them).
     Thanks to Ferran for the reports and the test document.
1.0  First release.
